              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ephippium, ephippiī — \"a saddle cloth, a horse blanket\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Servus ephippium in equum pōnit. The slave puts the saddle cloth on the horse."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Second declension, neuter: ephippium, ephippiī n. Riders sat on a padded cloth rather than a modern saddle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ephippium was borrowed from Greek ephippion 'saddlecloth', built from epi 'on' and hippos 'horse' (EtymDB; Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
