          "title": "You'll want to know: calcar, calcāris",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "calcar, calcāris — \"a spur\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Eques calcar habet, sed equus lentē it. The rider has a spur, but the horse goes slowly."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Third declension, neuter: calcar, calcāris n. Figurative too: a spur to effort."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "calcar is usually linked with calx, calcis 'heel': Lewis & Short compare calx and quote an ancient explanation that the spur is tied to the heel. EtymDB lists the word but gives no parent."
            }
          ]
        },
